course: dictionary
lesson: 5567
title: A word piece: ler
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some things you read are not whole words. «Ler» is one of them. On its own it is not a usual English word, but it is the end of longer words such as «butler», «sprinkler» and «tumbler». When you meet a small piece like this, look at the whole word it sits in.
explain: The same three letters can also be a name. Ler (also written Lir) is a sea god in old Irish stories, and «The Children of Lir» is about his children, who were turned into swans. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning is right.
explain: Other languages use pieces like this too. In Turkish, «the plural ending is -ler when the word's last vowel is e, i, ö or ü», so «kediler» means cats. Here -ler is a small ending added to a word, not a word by itself.
fact: A fragment is a small piece of something larger.
fact: «Ler» on its own is not a usual English word; it is the end of words like «butler», «sprinkler» and «tumbler».
fact: Ler (also written Lir) is a sea god in old Irish stories.
fact: «The Children of Lir» is a story about his children, who were turned into swans.
fact: In Turkish, -ler makes a plural when the last vowel is e, i, ö or ü, as in «kediler» (cats).
exercise: Which of these is a whole word that ends in «ler»? | timber | tumble | tumbling | *tumbler
exercise: In «The Children of Lir», what happens to Ler's children? | They sail a boat across the sea | They move to a school by the sea | *They are turned into swans | They become sea gods
exercise: In Turkish, «kedi» means cat. Which ending makes it mean more than one cat? | *-ler | -dir | -tan | -lar
test: In Turkish, which plural is correct for «kitap» (book), where the last vowel is a? | kitapsar | *kitaplar | kitapdan | kitapler
test: In Irish stories, what is Ler? | *A sea god | A kind of boat | A type of swan | A town by the sea
exam: Read this: «The sprinkler watered the lawn.» Is «ler» a piece of a word or a name here? | A Turkish plural ending | *A piece of the word sprinkler | A swan | A sea god
